                     Sekani Tribal Council, 2010 SCC 43, [2010] 2 S.C.R. 650; Law Society of Saskatchewan v. Abrametz, 2022 SCC 29, [2022] 2 S.C.R. 220; Housen v. Nikolaisen, <b>2002 SCC 33</b>, [2002] 2 S.C.R. 235; Canada (Transportation Safety Board) v. Carroll-Byrne, 2022 SCC 48; P. (W.) v. Alberta, 2014 ABCA 404, 378 D.L.R. (4th) 629; Toronto &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;Thus, the applicable standard of review is correctness (Housen v. Nikolaisen, <b>2002 SCC 33</b>, [2002] 2 S.C.R. 235, at para. 8). [32] That said, I would add the following for clarity. 
                </p>
